May 14, 2026 - Figure 03 completes 8-hour autonomous live stream

Research findings from YouTube and manufacturer sites:

- **Figure 03**: Just completed a landmark 8-hour fully autonomous live stream demonstration running Helix-02 AI. This is the first time a humanoid robot has demonstrated 8 hours of continuous autonomous operation at human performance levels. Major milestone for autonomy.

- Unitree G1: $13,500, available for direct US purchase via shop.unitree.com, but household chore capability (dishes, trash, laundry) NOT verified for base model. Still unclear if it can handle these autonomously.

- 1X NEO: $20,000, preorder available, but 1X CEO confirmed to WSJ that early units rely on human teleoperators when AI gets stuck.

- Figure AI: Best AI (Helix model), just demonstrated 8-hour continuous autonomous operation. But lease-only ($30K-$150K), no consumer purchase option.

- Tesla Optimus Gen 3: Production-line preparation ongoing, but consumer availability pushed to late 2027 per Musk.

- Boston Dynamics Atlas: Industrial focus, Hyundai partnership for factory work (2028), not for consumer sale.

- Sunday Memo: Targets dishes/laundry but beta not until Thanksgiving 2026, no pricing announced.

- SwitchBot Onero: Household robot on wheeled base (not humanoid), can do chores but doesn't qualify.

CONCLUSION: No robot meets ALL three criteria (US purchase availability, ≤$40K, household chore capability) as of May 14, 2026. Answer remains "No."
